the latest trailer for infinity war has  arrived and it's packed with even more  action than before with a ton of all-new  epic moments thundering across the  screen some less obvious details are  bound to slip through the cracks here  are the small details you may have  missed in the new infinity war trailer  half the universe while the first  trailer had Thanos waxing poetic about  his dream of balancing the universe it  was still pretty vague about just how he  intended to do that now Gamora spells  out for us exactly what he plans to do  he only ever had one goal to wipe out  half the universe if he gets all the  Infinity stones longtime comics readers  know what's up when Thanos assembled the  full power of the stones in the 1991  comic event Infinity Gauntlet his first  order of business was to make half of  all life in the universe suddenly  vanished without warning he did this in  order to impress Marvel's death who in  the comics is a sexy undead being he  would very much like the smoochy it  seems our heroes will have a bit more of  an advance warning in the movie but will  they be able to stop that oh s--- before  his fateful finger snap Loki's betrayal  in the last few minutes of Thor Ragnarok  Loki deftly lifted the tesseract  promotants treasure room as the Ascar d  ins journeyed into space away from the  ruins of their home Loki and Thor seemed  to at last truly make amends or did they  the new infinity war trailer finds the  god of mischief seemingly ready to  surrender the tesseract willingly the so  called space stone is likely what will  allow the mad Titan to warp to earth  what's Loki's endgame it's impossible to  guess considering he has a penchant for  double triple and quadruple crosses  surprise new order the black order is  Thanos's elite squad of lieutenants  charged with doing the kind of nitty  gritty dirty work he wouldn't touch with  a ten-foot Infinity Gauntlet their  on-screen incarnation includes  strategist Corvus glaive Proxima  midnight  the massive cull obsidian and the  slippery Evan Imam while we can only  glimpse the assembled group briefly in  the trailer every mall gets special  attention he may be in the midst of  manipulating the power of dr. strange to  facilitate Thanos invasion which is  something he's done before in the comics  tiny Gamora the two guardians of the  galaxy movies have built an epic  backstory a family drama behind Thanos  and his daughters Gamora and nebula it's  a bitter tale of abuse betrayal and  attempted murder the new infinity war  trailer provides a surprising moment of  family bonding we see fan OHS take a  tiny green hand in his giant purple one  as he walks with a young girl toward an  ornate archway it seems like a safe bet  that the girl is a young Gamora  but is this a flashback maybe some  weirdness via the Infinity stones  Thanos gets his helmet since his first  appearance during the end credits of the  Avengers Thanos's look has been tweaked  but he remains instantly recognizable  but when the first infinity war trailer  hit many comic book fans were plagued  with one question  where's his helmet something about that  big bald head just felt wrong  fortunately the new trailer shows off  multiple shots that find his shiny hat  firmly in place or freshly removed  where's Hawkeye Marvel is touting  infinity war as the culmination of the  entire Marvel Cinematic Universe  providing a grand clash of as many  heroes and villains as can fit into two  and a half hours of IMAX sized action I  know all your names  the new trailer includes just about all  of our leading stars but one of the  original Avengers is still conspicuously  missing Jeremy Renner is confirmed to be  back once more as Clint Barton aka  Hawkeye but none of infinity wars  marketing has shown even a single one of  Hawkeye's mighty purple feathers it  would be strange if this founding member  of the cinematic Avengers didn't have a  major role to play in this big payoff  directors Joe and Anthony Russo remained  tight-lipped on the subject of Clint  hinting only that he has a special spot  in the film let's hope he actually stays  alive and doesn't get well shafted  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our youtube channel  let's check out all this cool stuff we  know you love to  [Music]
 

